        "original_id": "25f1d17f-3c24-5963-8605-d0709a7ac066",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Noyce, Jack Kilby\n- Products: first integrated circuit, microchip\n- Companies: Texas Instruments\n- Places: Silicon Valley\n- Events: Nobel Prize in Physics\n- Topics: personal computer revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Jack St. Clair Kilby was born on November 8, 1923, and died on June 20, 2005.\n- In 1958, Jack Kilby took part in the realization of the first integrated circuit while working at Texas Instruments.\n- Robert Noyce is credited, along with Jack Kilby, with the realization of the first integrated circuit, or microchip.\n- The first integrated circuit helped fuel the personal computer revolution and contributed to Silicon Valley getting its name.\n- Jack Kilby was awarded the Nobel Prize in Physics on December 10, 2000.",
